README.md
    1→# OTree - Object Tree TUI Viewer
    5→A command line tool to view objects (JSON/YAML/TOML/XML) in TUI tree widget.
    7→## Install
    …
    9→Download binary files from [release page](https://github.com/fioncat/otree/releases).
    11→You can also build it from source (require `cargo` installed):
    13→```bash
    14→cargo install --git https://github.com/fioncat/otree
    15→```
    17→### Arch Linux (AUR)
    …
    25→### macOS and Linux (Homebrew)
    …
    33→## Usage
    …
    35→Open a JSON/YAML/TOML file in TUI tree viewer:
    37→```bash
    38→otree /path/to/file.json
    39→otree /path/to/file.yaml
    40→otree /path/to/file.toml
    41→otree /path/to/file.xml
    42→```
    44→For more command usage, please run `otree --help`.
    46→You can configure TUI keys, colors, and more in `~/.config/otree.toml`, the default configuration is [here](config/default.toml).
    48→For all available actions and their default key bindings, please refer to: [All Available Actions](docs/actions.md).
    50→For how to configure TUI colors, please refer to: [Colors Document](docs/colors.md).
    52→## Roadmap
    …
    82→## Thanks
    …
    84→I created this tool to better view those super deep YAML files of Kubernetes while [jnv](https://github.com/ynqa/jnv) only supports JSON.
    86→This is based on the amazing TUI framework [ratatui](https://github.com/ratatui-org/ratatui) and its tree widget [tui-tree-widget](https://github.com/EdJoPaTo/tui-rs-tree-widget.git).
